{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tom, Dick, and Harry are playing a game. Starting at the same time, each of them flips a fair coin repeatedly until he gets his first head, at which point he stops. What is the probability that all three flip their coins the same number of times?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de29a0e36ed3c428e6b87c2c0fed21cf406aa12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By: dragonfly\n</p><p>We can solve this problem by listing it as an infinite geometric equation. We get that to have the same amount of tosses, they have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> chance of getting all heads. Then the next probability is all of them getting tails and then on the second try, they all get heads. The probability of that happening is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fd5186d1addce37ab968f92438d9337dd1fea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"45\" height=\"46\" />.We then get the geometric equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c2811227d7e4e6d450dfc4eeb027a7fbae6e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{8}+\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)^3...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"202\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>And then we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> equals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5edf51fe473abbd5f4206cfef9858a86ee222aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"48\" /> because of the formula of the sum for an infinite series, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4afcfc1803d5483a5a035c630dbd5dab4c483918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{8}}{1-\\frac{1}{8}} = \\frac{1}{8}*\\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"149\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call it a \"win\" if the boys all flip their coins the same number of times, and the probability that they win is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that they win on their first flip is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. If they don't win on their first flip, that means they all flipped tails (which also happens with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> ) and that their chances of winning have returned to what they were at the beginning. This covers all possible sequences of winning flips. So we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a348dac001fa202e876891f8c4ba05cb010f98ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8}P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5edf51fe473abbd5f4206cfef9858a86ee222aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rLAcJe3o-uA?t=75\">https://youtu.be/rLAcJe3o-uA?t=75</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_.28Problem_11-20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fast Forward to 39:00 for problem 19\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o</a>\n</p><p>~THEMATHCANADIAN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B\">2016 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Pro